# The only variable you need to set.
#
# REQUIRED in production. Encrypts the session cookie that holds your Garmin
# token. Without it the app refuses to serve requests, because sessions would
# break as soon as the host runs more than one instance.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
APP_SECRET=

# --- Everything below is optional. Leave these commented out. ---
#
# Some hosts read this file and pre-create every key they find, which is why
# they are commented: an empty GARMIN_MOCK or GARMIN_DOMAIN is not what you
# want sitting in your deployment.

# Set to 1 to serve built-in sample data and never contact Garmin. Useful for
# working on the UI. Leave unset (or 0) to read your real Garmin account.
# GARMIN_MOCK=0

# Garmin's Chinese platform uses garmin.cn.
# GARMIN_DOMAIN=garmin.com

# The mobile-client OAuth credentials are fetched at runtime; set these to pin
# them instead.
# GARMIN_CONSUMER_KEY=
# GARMIN_CONSUMER_SECRET=
